contentText:
Kelly Clarkson, John Legend and Adam Levine return for a new season of The Voice: Battle of Champions. They share who they’re most excited to see return, what fans can expect from their performances together and more!

John Legend:

We&#8217;re also doing the all-star showdown this season, which is different. We&#8217;re bringing back some of our greatest artists from seasons past.

Kelly Clarkson:

Fighting for us for another spot in the final.&nbsp;

That&#8217;s right. Are we?&nbsp;

Elated?&nbsp;

We love truly, not just because she&#8217;s here. We truly love having Kelly back. She brings such great energy, such great expertise. She also is really difficult to beat.

Adam Levine:

She&#8217;s also, like, one of the best singers ever.

You know what I was going to say, look, I&#8217;ve toured with Adam. He&#8217;s one of the greatest singers live. He is insane live. I have seen you, John, live. You are insane. The showmanship, the level of writing and your voice. It&#8217;s so fun to cut like we were thinking about a song to sing all together. And there&#8217;s so many different types of artists, it&#8217;s kind of hard to pick a song. But I think all of us are based in soulfulness. It doesn&#8217;t matter the genre we all are soulful and whatever genre where we happen to be singing in, and we all love playing in different genres. It&#8217;s actually my favorite set of like, coaches to work with in that, in that sense, because it&#8217;s like.

Yeah, the musical taste, I think, between the three of us is very cohesive, yeah, like, and I think that&#8217;s it&#8217;s not, not that we haven&#8217;t shared tons in common with other, with other coaches as well. But like, this does feel like we come from a very similar place.

Basically, everyone be very excited for our coach performance. Yes, exactly. It&#8217;s gonna be nice.&nbsp;

Be excited.&nbsp;

Keep watching for more!
